# Canonical identities for PRISM contributors.
#
# Maps the aliases that appear in this repository's history to the authors
# ratified in pyproject.toml. Most entries exist because `user.email` was
# unset on a cluster node, so Git fell back to `user@<hostname>` -- Aurora
# UANs and compute nodes, Polaris logins, and so on. Others are GitHub
# noreply addresses or a misconfigured `Your Name <you@example.com>`.
#
# Generated from `git log --all`, so it covers every ref, not just main.
# `GitHub <noreply@github.com>` is deliberately absent: that is the web-UI
# committer on squash merges, not a person.
#
# Two consumers:
#   * `git shortlog -sne`, `git log --use-mailmap` and GitHub's contributor
#     views in this repository, which is where the aliased commits live.
#   * The AI-ModCon/PRISM release snapshot, which copies this file verbatim
#     (see tools/make_release_snapshot.sh). That repo has no history of its
#     own, so there the file records who the work came from rather than
#     something git resolves against.

